Error [E0507]: While the loop is reading `nums`, nothing may change it
  --> tests/ui/lambda_map_mutate_list.jet:5:13
    |
  5 |             nums.push(0)
    |             ^^^^
 Why: The loop reads `nums` across its body, so `nums.push()` can change the visited domain, element order, or termination.
 Fix: Choose the collection intent explicitly: use a separate result when the original traversal should stay unchanged; snapshot `nums` and iterate the fixed original set when only the original values belong in the traversal; or use an explicit work queue when newly added values should be visited. Do not use index traversal unless its fixed domain and result meaning are intended.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0507

